[Tiry a q-ul-Qul u b, R uha n i Khaz a ’in, vol. 15, pp. 507-511]
Persian Poem
O Mighty Lord, Creator of heaven and earth,
O Merciful, Compassionate and Guide;
Who looks into the hearts;
And from Whom nothing is hidden.
If You see that I am wicked and vicious;
If You have determined that I am evil;
Then break this evil one into pieces;
And gladden the hearts of my opponents.
Shower Thy mercy on their hearts;
Grant of Thy grace all their wishes.
Send down a blazing fire on the walls and doors of
my dwelling,
Be my enemy and destroy my work.
But if You do count me as one of Your servants;
And my attention is all concentrated on You;
And if You find my heart full of such love for You,
As is entirely unknown to the world;
Then deal with me by way of love;
And make manifest a little of its mystery.
O You Who comes towards every seeker;
And are aware of the yearning of every heart that is
aflame with Your love,
For the sake of the relationship that I have with
You;
